note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note Zero-copy buffer sharing over the NVIDIA RM client, ABI 580.173.02: the OM-2 function-mode unit
note for the one hosted native library (omega-bridge ABI v2, tools/native --host). It has the same
note export and import semantics as the program-mode native/share/share.om, which composes with
note native/nvrm/context.om globals. Function mode has no globals or texts, so all state lives in
note caller buffers: one zcshare block per shared buffer, the 24-byte zcrec share record, one
note 9264-byte parameter scratch (the largest request, UVM_MAP_EXTERNAL_ALLOCATION), and the
note control-device path for the fresh descriptor RM_MAP_MEMORY binds. The CPU mapping token lives
note in whichever native context the caller passes (omega2_ctx_nvshare_*); import and release
note must use the same context, and each live import holds one of its slots.
note Export grants DUP_OBJECT by RM_SHARE with the OS security token policy (same user only).
note Import duplicates the owner's memory with RM_DUP_OBJECT, proves its size, then maps it for
note the CPU and the GPU at the caller's address. Read-only imports set every access flag read-only.
note The duplicate holds its own reference: the pages outlive the owner's free or exit.
note Exports return 0, or the error that zcshare.err also records: a negative errno, or the
note positive RM status of a refused request. -5 faulted block, -16 block already holds an import,
note -22 malformed record or block, -34 size other than wanted or than the object, -75 address,
note -1 re-export of an import (EPERM); a slot shortage is maphold's -24.
om2
note Per-buffer block. Inputs: ctlfd, uvmfd, client, device, vaspace, uuid (from the NVRM client);
note export: obj (the owned memory handle) and size; import: newh (the handle the duplicate gets),
note mode (0 read/write, 1 read-only), size (the byte size wanted) and addr (CPU and GPU address).
note Outputs: obj (the live duplicate), map (the CPU mapping token), live (1 RM duplicate, 2 CPU
note mapping, 4 UVM range, 8 DMA mapping, 16 completed import), stage (51 export, 52 duplicate,
note 53 size proof and CPU map, 54 UVM range, 55 DMA map, 56 UVM external mapping, 57 imported),
note err and fault. fault is sticky: the RM view may differ from the block, as for a faulted
note context.om; the block is released with nvshare_release and then discarded.
layout zcshare 96
field ctlfd int at 0 little
field uvmfd int at 4 little
field client uint at 8 little
field device uint at 12 little
field vaspace uint at 16 little
field obj uint at 20 little
field newh uint at 24 little
field mode uint at 28 little
field size ulong at 32 little
field addr ulong at 40 little
field map long at 48 little
field live uint at 56 little
field stage uint at 60 little
field err long at 64 little
field uuid uchar 16 at 72 little
field fault uint at 88 little
end
note Share record, little endian: magic OMZC, version 1, owner client, owner memory handle,
note byte size (whole 4 KiB pages). Byte-identical to share.om's nvshrec.
layout zcrec 24
field magic uint at 0 little
field version uint at 4 little
field client uint at 8 little
field handle uint at 12 little
field size ulong at 16 little
end

fn zcz p edit uchar 9264 n ulong to void
for i ulong n
put p i 0
end
end
fn zcp32 p edit uchar 9264 off ulong v uint to void
for i ulong 4
put p add off i uchar and shr v mul i 8 255
end
end
fn zcg32 p edit uchar 9264 off ulong to uint
v = uint 0
for i ulong 4
v = or v shl uint get p add off i mul i 8
end
ret v
end
fn zcp64 p edit uchar 9264 off ulong v ulong to void
for i ulong 8
put p add off i uchar and shr v mul i 8 255
end
end
fn zcg64 p edit uchar 9264 off ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
for i ulong 8
v = or v shl ulong get p add off i mul i 8
end
ret v
end
fn zcfail s edit zcshare e long to long
put s err e
ret e
end
note A Linux result r and an RM status st: both zero, or record the first failure.
fn zcok s edit zcshare r long st uint to bool
if ne r 0
put s err r
ret false
end
if ne st 0
put s err long st
ret false
end
ret true
end
note Shareable sizes: whole 4 KiB pages, at most 64 GiB.
fn zcsize size ulong to bool
if or eq size 0 gt size 68719476736
ret false
end
ret eq and size 4095 0
end

note Publish one owned buffer: obj and size in s. Fills rec on success only.
note A block that holds an import is refused (EPERM): only the owner exports.
export fn nvshare_export s edit zcshare rec edit zcrec p edit uchar 9264 to long
if ne get s fault 0
ret zcfail s neg long 5
end
if ne and get s live 16 0
ret zcfail s neg long 1
end
h = get s obj
size = get s size
if or eq h 0 eq get s client 0
ret zcfail s neg long 22
end
if not zcsize size
ret zcfail s neg long 22
end
put s stage 51
zcz p 24
zcp32 p 0 get s client
zcp32 p 4 h
note RS_SHARE_POLICY: target 0, access mask bit RS_ACCESS_DUP_OBJECT, type OS security token, action 0.
zcp32 p 8 0
zcp32 p 12 1
zcp32 p 16 2
r = devctl get s ctlfd uint 3222816309 p 0 24
if not zcok s r zcg32 p 20
ret get s err
end
put rec magic 1129991503
put rec version 1
put rec client get s client
put rec handle h
put rec size size
put s err 0
ret long 0
end

note RM_FREE of the duplicate under the device. Clears live bit 1 on success; faults otherwise.
fn zcfree s edit zcshare p edit uchar 9264 to bool
zcz p 16
zcp32 p 0 get s client
zcp32 p 4 get s device
zcp32 p 8 get s obj
r = devctl get s ctlfd uint 3222292009 p 0 16
if not zcok s r zcg32 p 12
put s fault 1
ret false
end
put s live and get s live 4294967294
put s obj 0
ret true
end

note RM_MAP_MEMORY on the control device. Returns a negative errno or the RM status.
fn zcmap s edit zcshare p edit uchar 9264 obj uint off ulong n ulong fd long to long
zcz p 56
zcp32 p 0 get s client
zcp32 p 4 get s device
zcp32 p 8 obj
zcp64 p 16 off
zcp64 p 24 n
if eq get s mode 1
zcp32 p 44 1
end
zcp32 p 48 uint fd
r = devctl get s ctlfd uint 3224913486 p 0 56
if lt r 0
ret r
end
if gt r 0
ret neg long 5
end
ret long zcg32 p 40
end

note Size proof and CPU map. RM refuses a map that starts at or past the object's end
note (INVALID_BASE 0x20) and one that runs past it (INVALID_LIMIT 0x2e). A probe one page past
note the claimed end must be refused as INVALID_BASE, and the full claimed span must map.
note Either mismatch is -34 (ERANGE). Returns the mapping token, or -1 with err set. A
note mapping that cannot be dropped after a failed close stays in map with live bit 2.
fn zccpu s edit zcshare p edit uchar 9264 path view uchar * obj uint size ulong to long
fd = fopen path 0 len path 524290 0
if lt fd 0
put s err fd
ret neg long 1
end
st = zcmap s p obj size 4096 fd
if eq st 32
st = zcmap s p obj 0 size fd
if eq st 46
st = neg long 34
end
else
if eq st 0
st = neg long 34
end
end
if ne st 0
r = fclose int fd
if ne r 0
put s fault 1
end
put s err st
ret neg long 1
end
m = maphold get s addr size
if gt m 0
r = neg long 1
if eq get s mode 1
r = mapbind m int fd 0 1
else
r = mapbind m int fd 0 3
end
if ne r 0
m = r
end
end
r = fclose int fd
if ne r 0
put s err r
put s fault 1
if gt m 0
r = mapdrop m
if ne r 0
put s map m
put s live or get s live 2
end
end
ret neg long 1
end
if lt m 0
put s err m
ret neg long 1
end
ret m
end

note GPU side of an import, after the CPU map, as in nvalloc: UVM external range at the CPU
note address, DMA map at that fixed address, UVM external mapping. A failure faults the block
note and leaves its live bits for nvshare_release.
fn zcgpu s edit zcshare p edit uchar 9264 d uint size ulong va ulong to bool
put s stage 54
zcz p 24
zcp64 p 0 va
zcp64 p 8 size
r = uvmctl get s uvmfd uint 73 p 0 24
if not zcok s r zcg32 p 16
put s fault 1
ret false
end
put s live or get s live 4
put s stage 55
zcz p 64
zcp32 p 0 get s client
zcp32 p 4 get s device
zcp32 p 8 get s vaspace
zcp32 p 12 d
zcp64 p 24 size
fl = uint 33040
if eq get s mode 1
fl = 33041
end
zcp32 p 32 fl
zcp64 p 48 va
r = devctl get s ctlfd uint 3225437783 p 0 64
if not zcok s r zcg32 p 56
put s fault 1
ret false
end
put s live or get s live 8
if ne zcg64 p 48 va
put s err neg long 22
put s fault 1
ret false
end
put s stage 56
zcz p 9264
zcp64 p 0 va
zcp64 p 8 size
for i ulong 16
put p add i 24 get s uuid i
end
kind = uint 1
if eq get s mode 1
kind = 3
end
zcp32 p 40 kind
zcp64 p 9240 1
zcp32 p 9248 uint get s ctlfd
zcp32 p 9252 get s client
zcp32 p 9256 d
r = uvmctl get s uvmfd uint 33 p 0 9264
if not zcok s r zcg32 p 9260
put s fault 1
ret false
end
ret true
end

note Record and block checks before any RM call: 0, or the clean refusal to return.
fn zcchk s edit zcshare rec view zcrec to long
if ne get s fault 0
ret neg long 5
end
if ne get s live 0
ret neg long 16
end
if or ne get rec magic 1129991503 ne get rec version 1
ret neg long 22
end
if or eq get rec client 0 eq get rec handle 0
ret neg long 22
end
size = get rec size
if not zcsize size
ret neg long 22
end
if ne size get s size
ret neg long 34
end
if gt get s mode 1
ret neg long 22
end
if or eq get s newh 0 eq get s client 0
ret neg long 22
end
note maphold's bounds (64 KiB up to 1 TiB) also keep the GPU address below the VA space vaSize.
va = get s addr
if ne and va 4095 0
ret neg long 75
end
if or lt va 65536 gt va sub 1099511627776 size
ret neg long 75
end
ret long 0
end

note RM_DUP_OBJECT of the record's object under the device as newh. Returns the duplicate
note handle, or 0 with err set (fault too when RM accepted but returned handle 0).
fn zcdup s edit zcshare rec view zcrec p edit uchar 9264 to uint
zcz p 28
zcp32 p 0 get s client
zcp32 p 4 get s device
zcp32 p 8 get s newh
zcp32 p 12 get rec client
zcp32 p 16 get rec handle
zcp32 p 20 0
r = devctl get s ctlfd uint 3223078452 p 0 28
if not zcok s r zcg32 p 24
ret 0
end
d = zcg32 p 8
if eq d 0
put s err neg long 22
put s fault 1
end
ret d
end

note Import the buffer rec describes into s. Clean refusals leave no RM object or mapping and
note do not fault the block: malformed record or block -22, size other than wanted or than the
note object -34, address -75, slots full -24, RM refusal of the duplicate (wrong handle, not
note shared) the positive RM status. A returned duplicate handle 0 is -22 and faults.
export fn nvshare_import s edit zcshare rec view zcrec p edit uchar 9264 path view uchar * to long
e = zcchk s rec
if ne e 0
ret zcfail s e
end
size = get rec size
va = get s addr
put s stage 52
d = zcdup s rec p
if eq d 0
ret get s err
end
put s obj d
put s live 1
put s stage 53
m = zccpu s p path d size
if le m 0
e = get s err
if zcfree s p
put s err e
end
ret get s err
end
put s map m
put s live 3
if not zcgpu s p d size va
ret get s err
end
put s live 31
put s stage 57
put s err 0
ret long 0
end

note Undo an import in nvmrel's order: UVM free, DMA unmap, RM free, CPU unmap. Each live bit
note clears only after its step is confirmed; a refused step faults the block and keeps the rest
note live for a retry. With nothing live it returns 0. fault stays set.
export fn nvshare_release s edit zcshare p edit uchar 9264 to long
va = get s addr
size = get s size
if ne and get s live 4 0
zcz p 24
zcp64 p 0 va
zcp64 p 8 size
r = uvmctl get s uvmfd uint 34 p 0 24
if not zcok s r zcg32 p 16
put s fault 1
ret get s err
end
put s live and get s live 4294967291
end
if ne and get s live 8 0
zcz p 48
zcp32 p 0 get s client
zcp32 p 4 get s device
zcp32 p 8 get s vaspace
zcp32 p 12 get s obj
zcp64 p 24 va
zcp64 p 32 size
r = devctl get s ctlfd uint 3224389208 p 0 48
if not zcok s r zcg32 p 40
put s fault 1
ret get s err
end
put s live and get s live 4294967287
end
if ne and get s live 1 0
if not zcfree s p
ret get s err
end
end
if ne and get s live 2 0
r = mapdrop get s map
if ne r 0
put s fault 1
ret zcfail s r
end
end
put s live 0
put s map 0
put s obj 0
put s stage 0
put s err 0
ret long 0
end
